    "# BigDecimal's C half, written in Ruby for mere-ruby.\n" ++
    "#\n" ++
    "# The reference's `require \"bigdecimal\"` reads the gem's bigdecimal.rb, which\n" ++
    "# requires 'bigdecimal.so' -- the C extension (ext/bigdecimal/bigdecimal.c,\n" ++
    "# bigdecimal 4.0.1). mere-ruby cannot load a C extension, so this file is\n" ++
    "# what 'bigdecimal.so' is here. It defines what the extension defines: the\n" ++
    "# BigDecimal class with its constants and methods, Kernel#BigDecimal, and the\n" ++
    "# thread-local modes. The gem's Ruby half (power, sqrt, BigMath) is shipped as\n" ++
    "# it is and runs on top of it.\n" ++
    "#\n" ++
    "# A value is a sign, an Integer coefficient and a power of ten: c * 10**e,\n" ++
    "# with c kept free of trailing zeros. Zero, the infinities and NaN are their\n" ++
    "# own kinds. Sums and products are exact, as the extension's are; a quotient\n" ++
